<p>Iran said the Strait of Hormuz would remain under &quot;strict control&quot; and again closed it to commercial shipping, reversing a brief reopening after the United States said its naval blockade of Iranian ports would stay in place until Tehran reached a deal. Multiple outlets also said Iranian forces fired on or attacked ships trying to pass through the waterway, including an Indian-flagged crude vessel, adding fresh danger to one of the world’s most important energy routes. Even so, both sides signaled that diplomacy is still alive. President Trump said Iran could not &quot;blackmail&quot; the United States while also describing recent contacts as &quot;very good conversations&quot;; Iranian negotiators said the talks had produced some progress, but fundamental differences remain over nuclear issues and the strait. The stakes reach well beyond the Gulf: Reuters-based reporting cited by several outlets said the conflict has already removed more than 500 million barrels of crude and condensate from the global market since late February, with analysts calling it the largest energy supply disruption in modern history.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/2otJr2u-ekxhjniJ4keKFD-0O-QbeZ1WjNvk8EsAenb3aWlYXgQy9GSp6rXFVYxe_tdjfnNG1NUd9P8F-lofYagotQzStudsrIOXZnxGw-m16jjNvXLDoJW7H5bZKYe7H08w-_wNPB8dOHAjgfTuHPc7oW9QZKZSJRnrBLDz7Gs_oF8iKgfRAQ_5U5TfqXKAI7ODdDLkGTaVFAxOiglnFNwLLjXHtQuTBcOzc11SUmR2Go25t3sT-kPb' alt='Tankers anchored in the Strait of Hormuz on Saturday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>India wording: India’s foreign ministry said it &quot;called in&quot; Iran’s envoy after the incident, and the envoy undertook to convey New Delhi’s request that Tehran resume facilitating India-bound ships across the strait.</li><li>Backchannel channel: Iran’s Supreme National Security Council said Pakistan’s army chief Asim Munir brought new U.S. proposals during a recent Tehran visit, a sign that talks are still moving through regional intermediaries.</li><li>Ceasefire clock: One report said the current ceasefire in the US-Israeli war against Iran is fragile and set to expire within days, raising pressure on negotiators to find at least a temporary arrangement.</li><li>Value of lost output: Reuters calculations cited by The Guardian say more than $50bn worth of crude has gone unproduced since the war began.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian negotiators: Iran’s top negotiator said recent contacts with Washington brought some progress, but major gaps remain, especially on nuclear issues and the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/trump-iran-cite-progress-talks-uncertainty-hangs-over-strait'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>President Trump: President Trump said Tehran could not use the strait to &quot;blackmail&quot; Washington, even as he described U.S.-Iran contacts as &quot;very good conversations,&quot; pairing public pressure with public optimism. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-iran-cite-progress-in-talks-as-uncertainty-hangs-over-strait'>Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Iranian officials: Iranian leaders called the U.S. naval blockade of Iranian ports a &quot;clumsy and ignorant decision,&quot; signaling that maritime pressure is central to the negotiations, not a side issue. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/18/iran-reasserts-control-of-hormuz-strait-as-trump-warns-against-blackmail'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Analysts: Reuters-based reporting cited by The Guardian said the aftershocks from the lost oil output may be felt for months or even years, suggesting the market damage could outlast the immediate military confrontation. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/19/middle-east-crisis-live-iran-us-strait-of-hormuz-trump-lebanon-israel'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/apr/19/middle-east-crisis-live-iran-us-strait-of-hormuz-trump-lebanon-israel'>Middle East crisis live: Iran says ‘fundamental’ issues’ still to be resolved with US amid strait of Hormuz impasse</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-cant-blackmail-us-trump-after-tehrans-flip-flop-on-strait-of-hormuz-11376420#publisher=newsstand'>&quot;They Got A Little Cute&quot;: Trump After Iran&#x27;s Flip-Flop On Strait Of Hormuz</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-trump-says-tehran-cannot-blackmail-us/live-76839599'>Iran war: Trump says Tehran cannot &#x27;blackmail us&#x27;</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/b45b0ebe-7f8c-40f3-a804-303aba404e22'>Iran claims ‘strict control’ of Strait of Hormuz and says it will not be fully reopened</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-iran-reimposes-restrictions-on-strait-of-hormuz-accusing-us-of/'>Iran reimposes restrictions on Strait of Hormuz, accusing U.S. of violating deal to reopen it</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/18/world/iran-us-war-trump-hormuz'>Tensions Rise in Strait of Hormuz Over Ship Attacks and Iranian Threats</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/04/19/iran-says-deal-still-far-off-as-hormuz-strait-remains-shut'>Iran says deal still &#x27;far off&#x27; as Hormuz Strait remains shut</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/Middle-East/2026/0418/iran-hormuz-us-ships'>Iran closes Strait of Hormuz again over US blockade and fires on ships</a> - csmonitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-israel-lebanon-ceasefire-hezbollah-strait-hormuz/'>Iran fires on ships in Strait of Hormuz as it closes the critical chokepoint again</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/4/19/iran-war-live-tehran-says-no-date-set-for-us-talks-hormuz-strait-closed'>Iran war live: Tehran says no date set for US talks, Hormuz Strait closed</a> - aljazee